WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:01.890
- [Narrator] Meme-inspired cryptocurrency

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:03.828
is shaking up the investing world.

00:00:03.828 --> 00:00:04.661
(glass shattering)

00:00:04.661 --> 00:00:07.680
In October, the meme coin
Shiba Inu dramatically surged

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:12.310
in value, growing over 1,100%
in the span of 30 days.

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:15.583
And eventually reaching a market
cap of around $41 billion.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:18.670
- I think we've seen examples

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:21.340
where someone put a little bit of money

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:23.830
into something like Doge
or Shiba very early on

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:25.660
and then they became
millionaires over night.

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:27.420
- [Narrator] Shiba Inu's metric rise

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.330
and subsequence fall is part

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:31.570
of a growing trend of meme coins,

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:33.660
a category of cryptocurrencies inspired

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:37.890
by popular social media
jokes, sarcasm or puns.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:41.380
I got $17 of Dogecoin as a joke in 2017.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:43.300
Not it's worth 800 bucks.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.150
- [Instructor] Their surge
in popularity reflects

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:47.970
the behaviors of a growing
class of crypto traders

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:50.080
that are making a
surprisingly large impact

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:51.460
on market prices.

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:53.760
- I think they see it as a good way

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:55.220
to make money quickly,

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:59.050
and sort of try their hands
at the investing game.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:01.820
- [Narrator] But what's led
to the growth of meme coins?

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:03.740
And what trends are they helping to shape

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:06.220
in the world of cryptocurrency?

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:10.000
- So meme coins are basically
like the meme stocks

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.670
of the cryptocurrency world.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:14.700
So they are cryptocurrencies that tend

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:19.270
to rise really quickly and
really sharply in value largely

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:22.000
because of buzz online.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.550
- [Narrator] To understand the
roots of the meme coin craze,

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.730
you have to go back to 2013.

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:29.350
That's when Dogecoin
was created as a joke,|

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:32.180
playing off the popular
Shiba Inu dog meme.

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:33.610
At its all-time high,

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:37.280
the value of Dogecoin
surged more than 15,000%

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:38.610
for the year.

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:41.030
- So that means if you'd
put $100 into Dogecoin

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:42.830
at the start of the year,

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:44.790
you would have ended up with that turning

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:47.190
into more than $15,000.

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:49.300
- [Narrator] Even though
Dogecoin was initially created

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:51.610
as a joke, many grew to consider it

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:54.170
a legitimate investment prospect.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:56.560
- Dogecoin sort of became the test case

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:58.200
for meme coins,

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.450
and that's really helped lead to the rise

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:03.110
of other meme coins, like Shiba Inu.

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:04.440
- [Narrator] Today, there are hundreds

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:06.660
of different meme-inspired
cryptocurrencies,

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:07.930
and in order to stand out,

00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:09.820
effective branding is key.

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:12.080
Meme coins are very community driven,

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:13.530
meaning social media hype,

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:17.280
publicity and viral moments
largely drive their success.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:20.200
For instance, Tesla CEO Elon Musk

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.790
has posted regular tweets about Dogecoin,

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:24.600
often contributing to sudden surges

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:26.490
in meme coin prices.

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:28.940
- So in addition to seeing this rise

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:30.190
of meme coins this year,

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:32.680
we have also seen this subset within that

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:35.030
of dog coins sort of taking off.

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:36.870
So we first had Dogecoin,

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:38.270
then we had Shiba Inu.

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:39.530
And then recently, we've seen a lot

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:42.820
of speculation and
excitement around Floki Inu.

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:47.120
And that is because Elon
Musk has a Shiba Inu dog

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:49.310
that he has named Floki.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:50.750
- [Narrator] Another attractive aspect

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:54.160
of meme coins is their
tendency to be very cheap.

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:57.310
While one Bitcoin costs around $57,000,

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.760
a Shiba Inu coin is just a tiny fraction

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:01.200
of one cent.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.980
As Bitcoin, Ether and other
established cryptocurrencies

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:05.800
become more expensive,

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:07.760
cheaper coins offer an opportunity

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:09.790
to make quick gains.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:12.530
And while all cryptocurrency
investments are risky,

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:15.110
meme coins are particularly volatile,

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:17.090
prone to double-digit percentage swings

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:19.080
in a single day.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:21.600
- People tend to hold Bitcoin a bit longer

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:24.960
than they do Shiba or Dogecoin.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:27.980
And so I think that can
add to a lot of volatility.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:29.640
- [Narrator] One reason
for this volatility

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:32.090
is a lack of built-in scarcity.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:33.460
Bitcoin has a finite supply

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:35.330
of 21 million coins,

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:38.120
creating value similar to
the way gold is valuable

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:39.970
because it's scarce.

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:42.760
Meanwhile, many meme
coins are inflationary,

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:46.560
meaning they have unlimited
or extremely high supply caps.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.220
Shiba Inu, for instance,

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:50.950
started with a cap of
one quadrillion coins.

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:53.570
That's one million billions.

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:56.440
Over time, a nearly
unlimited cap on supply

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:58.660
can negatively impact value.

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:03.660
- There's a cap on the number
of Bitcoin in existence,

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.770
and people might be incentivized

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:08.270
to hold it a bit longer.

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:10.450
- [Narrator] Many investors
will trade meme coins

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:13.280
like Doge or Shiba Inu
on a short-term basis,

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:15.120
hoping to make a quick profit.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:17.500
So while it is possible
to make money investing

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:20.680
in meme coins, this type
of investment is risky,

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:22.590
and can be more similar to gambling

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:24.160
than true investing.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.560
- Investors need to be cognizant

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:28.240
of making sure they're
investing in something

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:29.700
that is legitimate.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:33.900
We have seen scams happening
in the altcoin world

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:36.140
just because I think everyone right now

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:39.170
is very eager to find the next Dogecoin

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:40.600
or find the next Bitcoin.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:41.920
- [Narrator] Something else to consider

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:44.750
when investing in meme coins is utility.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:49.000
- So I think the big proponents
of Bitcoin find a lot

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.783
of value in it because it is something

00:04:51.783 --> 00:04:52.990
that can be used

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:55.660
to transact in the real world.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:57.520
I think the difference with meme coins

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:01.181
is that there isn't as
much real-world value.

00:05:01.181 --> 00:05:04.320
- [Narrator] While the future
of meme coins is uncertain,

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.160
their rise in popularity reveals

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:08.690
that even the most unconventional trades

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:11.220
can lead to some of the largest gains.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:12.680
- It's hard to say

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:15.900
when this phenomenon will die
down or if it will die down.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:19.140
I think retail investors have
been a much stickier base

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:20.880
than people were anticipating.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.160
I think it's gonna be really interesting

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:25.263
and exciting to watch.

00:05:25.263 --> 00:05:27.930
(pensive music)

